# .gitignore for the dev plugin
#
# Rule of thumb: commit what a person wrote and needs to rebuild the project.
# Ignore anything a tool generates, anything specific to one machine, and
# anything secret. Each section says why it's here.

# --- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# These should never reach a remote. If one ever does, rotate it first, then
# purge it from history. Removing the file in a later commit doesn't help,
# because history keeps it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.netrc
credentials*.json
secrets.*

# --- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
# Bytecode and build output are regenerated on every run. Committing them
# causes noisy diffs and merge conflicts.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Tool caches ---------------------------------------------------------
# Linters, type checkers and test runners keep local caches to speed up the
# next run. They belong to one machine, not to the project.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Infrastructure ------------------------------------------------------
# Terraform state can contain secrets in plain text and must live in a
# remote backend, never in git. .terraform/ holds downloaded providers.
# Do commit .terraform.lock.hcl: it pins provider versions, the same way a
# Python lock file pins packages.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log

# --- Claude Code: local and per-user files ------------------------------
# settings.local.json holds personal permission overrides. Skill eval runs
# create large throwaway workspaces.
.claude/settings.local.json
*-workspace/
evals/**/runs/

# --- Logs and scratch ----------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
tmp/
scratch/

# --- OS and editor clutter ----------------------------------------------
# Files your OS or editor creates. Many engineers put these in a global
# gitignore (git config --global core.excludesFile) instead, since they
# aren't about this project. Listing them here also protects contributors
# who haven't set that up.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
